      "starterCode": "import csv\n# Read transactions.csv, filter 'SETTLED', compute sum and write settled.csv\n",
      "desc": "Filter rows where status == 'SETTLED'. Calculate settled_total and write settled rows to settled.csv with DictWriter.",
      "prompt": "<strong>[Hard] Transforming and Filtering CSV Data</strong><p>Populate <code>transactions.csv</code> with 4 sample rows. Filter records where <code>status == 'SETTLED'</code>, accumulate the sum of their float amounts into <code>settled_total</code>, and write these rows to <code>settled.csv</code> using <code>csv.DictWriter</code>. Record the count in <code>settled_count</code>.</p>",
      "ref": "import csv\nraw = 'tx_id,amount,status\\ntx_1,150.25,SETTLED\\ntx_2,89.00,PENDING\\ntx_3,220.50,SETTLED\\ntx_4,45.00,FAILED\\n'\nwith open('transactions.csv', 'w', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write(raw)\nsettled_rows = []\nsettled_total = 0.0\nwith open('transactions.csv', 'r', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if row['status'] == 'SETTLED':\n            settled_rows.append(row)\n            settled_total += float(row['amount'])\nwith open('settled.csv', 'w', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=['tx_id', 'amount', 'status'])\n    writer.writeheader()\n    writer.writerows(settled_rows)\nsettled_count = len(settled_rows)\n",
      "solution": "import csv\nraw = 'tx_id,amount,status\\ntx_1,150.25,SETTLED\\ntx_2,89.00,PENDING\\ntx_3,220.50,SETTLED\\ntx_4,45.00,FAILED\\n'\nwith open('transactions.csv', 'w', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write(raw)\nsettled_rows = []\nsettled_total = 0.0\nwith open('transactions.csv', 'r', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if row['status'] == 'SETTLED':\n            settled_rows.append(row)\n            settled_total += float(row['amount'])\nwith open('settled.csv', 'w', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=['tx_id', 'amount', 'status'])\n    writer.writeheader()\n    writer.writerows(settled_rows)\nsettled_count = len(settled_rows)\n",
